# Meridian Voice Concierge

- Spec: `docs/requirements.md`. Work items: `docs/tasks/` — read the relevant task file and meet its acceptance criteria. Reference requirement IDs (e.g. API-1, NF-5) in commit messages.
- Repository layout: follow `docs/project-structure.md`. Update that document when the layout changes.
- Services: `backend/` (FastAPI, sole owner of the database), `agent/` (LiveKit Agents, Python), `web/` (React: playground + admin). Each service has its own dependency manifest.
- `docker-compose.yml` and `.env.example` live at the repository root. Dockerfiles live in `deploy/local/`, not in service folders. Run the stack with `docker compose up --build`.
- The agent talks to the backend only over HTTP. Nothing outside `backend/` connects to the database.
- Configuration comes only from environment variables; every variable is listed in `.env.example` (copy to `./.env`). Never commit secrets or `.env` files.
- Do not build out-of-scope features: guest or admin authentication, bookings, payments, PMS integration, multi-language, mobile.
- Record non-obvious technical decisions in `docs/technical-decisions.md`.

## Non-functional requirements

- NF-1 Prompt responses: no blocking work on the agent's turn path; streaming STT/TTS; FAQ search should answer in under ~300 ms.
- NF-2 Docker: the full system runs with Docker Compose on a clean machine; migrations and seeding are automatic.
- NF-3 Admin UI targets desktop browsers.
- NF-4 Tone: guest-facing text is warm and professional — no slang, emojis, or markdown in spoken output.
- NF-5 Runtime settings (active voice) are read from the backend at the start of each session; changing them never requires a restart.
